# Playwright Test Authoring Rules (apps/med)

These rules apply to any code under `apps/med/tests/`. They exist because tests
that violate them become flaky, silently skip, or pass for the wrong reason.

## Selector priority (top first)

1. **`page.getByRole(role, { name })`** — primary. Works in EN and VI.
2. **`page.getByLabel(/regex/)`** — for form fields.
3. **`page.getByTestId('foo')`** — fall back to `data-testid` ONLY when 1–2 fail.
4. **`page.getByText(/regex/i)`** — last resort. Always case-insensitive regex.

NEVER use:

- CSS `.class-name` selectors (Tailwind classes change every build)
- `nth-child` indices
- XPath
- `page.locator('div > span')` chains

If a stable selector doesn't exist in the component, the **fix is to add a
`data-testid`** to the component in `apps/med/components/`, not to write a
brittle CSS selector.

## Wait strategy

- ✅ `await expect(locator).toBeVisible()` — auto-retries to default timeout
- ✅ `await page.waitForURL(/regex/)`
- ✅ `await page.waitForResponse(...)` for network-dependent assertions
- ❌ `await page.waitForTimeout(N)` — NEVER except as a brief debounce after a
  click that triggers an animation (cap at 500ms). Comment WHY.

## Tags are mandatory

Every `test.describe` block MUST declare:

- exactly one **layer** tag (`@smoke`, `@regression`, `@happy-path`, `@exploration`)
- exactly one **scope** tag (`@module-N` or `@cross-cutting`)
- at least one **concern** tag (`@a11y`, `@content`, `@state`, `@nav`, `@i18n`,
  `@visual`, `@data`, `@auth`, `@audio`)

Use `TAG.x` from `tests/e2e/_shared/tags.ts` — never hardcode the strings.

## Bug-traceability

If a test exists to prevent a regression from the user feedback xlsx, its
filename MUST be `bug-NNN-slug.spec.ts` and the describe block MUST include
`bugTag(NNN)`. This lets `/qa-triage` map a failure back to a user-reported
issue automatically.

## DB writes are forbidden in non-data tests

Tests under `tests/e2e/smoke/`, `tests/e2e/regression/` (UI-only), and
`tests/e2e/module-*/happy-path/` MUST NOT write to Supabase. They may only
READ via `getSupabaseAdmin()` for assertions.

Tests that DO seed data must:

1. Live under `tests/e2e/regression/` or `tests/e2e/data/`
2. Always clean up in an `afterEach` or `afterAll` (use try/finally)
3. Use the test user's UUID, never a hardcoded uuid

## fixme vs skip vs failing

- `test.fixme(...)` — known broken, captures a bug we WANT to fail once the
  app is fixed. The body still runs in `--grep @smoke` so reviewers see it.
- `test.skip(...)` — conditionally not applicable (e.g. requires env credentials)
- `test.fail(...)` — DO NOT USE. It hides real regressions.

## Console errors are failures

Smoke tests MUST register `page.on('pageerror', ...)` and
`page.on('console', msg => msg.type() === 'error')`, and assert empty at the
end. Tutorial-tour bugs and the audio-overlap bug both surface as console
errors first.

## Storage state, not re-login

Authenticated tests MUST start with:

```ts
import path from 'path';
const authFile = path.resolve('tests', '.auth', 'learner.json');
test.use({ storageState: authFile });
```

Never re-run the login form inside individual specs — that's what
`global.setup.ts` is for.

## Adding a new spec checklist

Before committing a new `*.spec.ts`:

- [ ] Filename matches `kebab-case.spec.ts` (or `bug-NNN-slug.spec.ts`)
- [ ] All three tag categories declared (layer / scope / concern)
- [ ] No `waitForTimeout` beyond 500ms (with a comment)
- [ ] No CSS class selectors
- [ ] No DB writes outside `regression/` or `data/`
- [ ] Runs locally with `npm run test:e2e -- <file>`
- [ ] `npm run test:coverage` regenerated and the gap row shrunk
